1
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:21,639
[SPEAKER_02]: This is from Samyuttinikāya, 56, 30, with Gavampati.

2
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:27,543
[SPEAKER_02]: At one time, several bhikkhus were staying in the land of the Chettis at Sahajati.

3
00:00:28,292 --> 00:00:37,095
[SPEAKER_02]: Now, at that time, after the meal, on return from alms round, several senior bhikkhus sat together in the pavilion, and this discussion came up among them.

4
00:00:37,816 --> 00:00:46,959
[SPEAKER_02]: Friends, does someone who sees suffering also see the origin of suffering, the cessation of suffering, and the practice that leads to the cessation of suffering?

5
00:00:47,698 --> 00:00:56,021
[SPEAKER_02]: When they said this, Venerable Gavampati said to those senior bhikkhus, Friends, I have heard and learned this in the presence of the Buddha.

6
00:00:56,801 --> 00:01:04,764
[SPEAKER_02]: Someone who sees suffering also sees the origin of suffering, the cessation of suffering, and the practice that leads to the cessation of suffering.

7
00:01:05,445 --> 00:01:13,287
[SPEAKER_02]: Someone who sees the origin of suffering also sees suffering, the cessation of suffering, and the practice that leads to the cessation of suffering.

8
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:17,269
[SPEAKER_02]: Someone who sees the cessation of suffering also sees suffering,

9
00:01:17,713 --> 00:01:21,875
[SPEAKER_02]: The origin of suffering and the practice that leads to the cessation of suffering.

10
00:01:22,495 --> 00:01:30,940
[SPEAKER_02]: Someone who sees the practice that leads to the cessation of suffering, also sees suffering, the origin of suffering, and the cessation of suffering.

11
00:01:40,805 --> 00:01:45,207
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's not something that's commonly known, is it?

12
00:01:45,467 --> 00:01:47,328
[SPEAKER_00]: Because usually there's a

13
00:01:48,689 --> 00:01:54,278
[SPEAKER_00]: It's sort of a... we naturally begin with this assumption that we all know what suffering is, kind of thing.

14
00:01:54,999 --> 00:02:00,448
[SPEAKER_00]: Or, maybe some people also assume they already know the practice that leads to the decision

15
00:02:03,539 --> 00:02:05,959
[SPEAKER_00]: There's a cessation for themselves, or something like that.

16
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:14,541
[SPEAKER_00]: After a period of doing the practice, you get this experience where you see the other truths that you didn't see before.

17
00:02:15,581 --> 00:02:16,682
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's actually more...

18
00:02:17,642 --> 00:02:25,243
[SPEAKER_00]: These things are so inextricably tied together, that if you see one, you automatically see the other one.

19
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:28,064
[SPEAKER_00]: So, first off, with suffering,

20
