00:12:13,687 --> 00:12:15,208
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no.

96
00:12:16,348 --> 00:12:23,970
[SPEAKER_01]: Until the four Noble Truths are seen, one basically doesn't know what the practice is, which means that you cannot mechanically settle

97
00:12:25,450 --> 00:12:31,633
[SPEAKER_01]: And continue doing what you think is right, because otherwise you would have seen all those Four Noble Truths already.

98
00:12:32,553 --> 00:12:51,322
[SPEAKER_01]: So, rather than accumulating more information, or thinking that the Four Noble Truths are the answer to a problem, it's actually more a question of, as you just said, like inquiry, and learning how to question, and be with the problem, even if it is unpleasant,

99
00:12:51,822 --> 00:13:03,486
[SPEAKER_01]: And basically learning how to not move away from it, because the mental movement away from it, will inevitably involve craving for or against the present situation that you find yourself in.

