104
00:13:45,474 --> 00:13:48,835
[SPEAKER_04]: Actually, that's a great exemplification of how it's timeless.

105
00:13:48,875 --> 00:13:52,037
[SPEAKER_04]: Like, if you see the problem, you already saw the cessation.

106
00:13:52,117 --> 00:13:52,657
[SPEAKER_04]: That's it, yeah.

107
00:13:59,647 --> 00:14:07,594
[SPEAKER_04]: If you have seen the cessation of craving, understood the Four Noble Truths, then you get access to this path.

108
00:14:10,401 --> 00:14:15,164
[SPEAKER_04]: Fully cement that cessation of craving, so that you never go back to it.

109
00:14:16,165 --> 00:14:23,649
[SPEAKER_04]: And that's why it says the the the suttas define like the the stream enterer, and then the the Buddha defines what it what is that stream.

110
00:14:24,509 --> 00:14:26,531
[SPEAKER_00]: And it says it's the no waitful path.

111
00:14:26,651 --> 00:14:29,172
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, so that's the stream that they enter.

112
00:14:29,392 --> 00:14:32,094
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, on account of having understood what

113
00:14:33,262 --> 00:14:41,995
[SPEAKER_04]: So, the reality is, they're able to practice this path, such that, while they're walking that path, craving is not there.

114
00:14:42,276 --> 00:14:47,965
