[SPEAKER_04]: Satipaṭṭhāna gets to the point where they're so familiar with that cessation of craving, that it doesn't come back.

122
00:15:33,331 --> 00:15:35,234
[SPEAKER_04]: Cessation of suffering, that it doesn't come back.

123
00:15:36,235 --> 00:15:40,019
[SPEAKER_04]: So, eh... that's an important thing to realize, because

124
00:15:42,490 --> 00:15:55,033
[SPEAKER_04]: We should understand that it's not... we shouldn't be mistaken for specific states of anger, or aversion, or sensuality, or desire.

125
00:15:55,673 --> 00:16:00,294
[SPEAKER_00]: Because these are more like the results of you not seeing your craving and acting out of it.

126
00:16:00,354 --> 00:16:04,475
[SPEAKER_00]: Then you get these very coarse sort of manifestations.

127
00:16:04,555 --> 00:16:10,297
[SPEAKER_00]: But really, even when your mind is calm and nothing's going on, craving is still there.

128
00:16:10,377 --> 00:16:11,877
[SPEAKER_04]: Because craving is

129
00:16:12,557 --> 00:16:15,659
[SPEAKER_04]: You could almost equate it with ignorance.

130
00:16:15,699 --> 00:16:18,160
[SPEAKER_04]: Craving just means not understanding.

131
00:16:19,561 --> 00:16:21,562
[SPEAKER_00]: Feelings means craving is there.

132
00:16:22,082 --> 00:16:36,490
[SPEAKER_04]: So, even when it's just a neutral feeling, that nothing's really happening, nothing's really bothering you, the fact that you don't see, that you don't understand, as the Buddha said, the gratification, the danger and the escape from these feelings, means that there is craving.

133
00:16:37,951 --> 00:16:41,234
[SPEAKER_04]: And again, that's timeless.

134
00:16:41,274 --> 00:16:43,756
[SPEAKER_04]: It's a timeless relationship.

135
00:16:45,378 --> 00:16:47,219
[SPEAKER_04]: So, yeah, that should be the practice.

136
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:54,726
[SPEAKER_04]: And, of course, all of this becomes apparent through the graduate training that comes before.

137
00:16:54,746 --> 00:17:00,631
[SPEAKER_04]: Because, as you just mentioned, you have to, to some extent, expose yourself

138
00:17:00,631 --> 00:17:10,239
